  "id": "Compound::DB00536 - Gene::3748",
  "verbalization": "Guanidine appears to interact with Kcnc3 through a shared pathway involving delayed rectifier potassium channels. The evidence suggests that Guanidine binds to Kcna6 or Kcnv2, which then participate in delayed rectifier potassium channel activity, ultimately leading to Kcnc3 being involved in this process. This indicates a potential mechanism where Guanidine influences potassium channel function, possibly through binding to specific subunits and modulating their activity. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a robust relationship, though the exact molecular mechanism remains to be fully elucidated. The involvement of multiple Kcna/Kcnv subunits highlights the complexity of the interaction, and further studies would be needed to determine the precise role of Guanidine in regulating Kcnc3 function.",
